# Sensor Changelog: AprilTag Rework

Date: 2026-06-15
Branch: sun/apriltag-2

Historical note: this entry describes the last shell-managed bring-up revision.
Current system startup uses `ros2 launch jmu_lunabotics master.launch.py`.

## Summary

Reworked the AprilTag detection stack so it is more resilient during bring-up
and shutdown. The update adds a stronger master launch path for sensor
processes and reimplements the AprilTag pipeline around calibrated camera
inputs, image rectification, and camera-relative pose/distance publishing.

## Master Launcher Updates

At that point, the sensor launcher acted as a stronger master process for the
camera and AprilTag stack.

It now:

- starts the camera publisher first
- conditionally starts the AprilTag publisher
- exports the shared camera and AprilTag configuration into child processes
- tracks background process IDs explicitly
- performs reinforced cleanup on exit, `Ctrl-C`, or termination signals

This reduces the chance of leaving orphaned camera or AprilTag processes behind
after a failed bring-up or interrupted run.

## AprilTag Detection Reimplementation

The AprilTag pipeline in:

```text
sensor/webcam/publish_apriltag.sh
```

was reimplemented so that it no longer assumes raw camera imagery is sufficient
for pose work.

The new flow is:

```text
/camera/image_raw
/camera/camera_info
    -> image_proc rectify_node
    -> /camera/image_rect
    -> apriltag_ros
```

This version:

- validates that `apriltag_ros` and `image_proc` are installed
- generates its detector configuration at launch time
- waits for the rectified image topic before starting AprilTag detection
- publishes detections under the `/apriltag` namespace
- keeps tag family, tag ID, and tag size configurable from environment

## Camera-Relative Pose Output

The AprilTag system now includes:

```text
sensor/webcam/publish_apriltag_pose.py
```

This helper listens to the detected AprilTag transform path and republishes:

```text
/apriltag/camera_pose
/apriltag/camera_distance
```

The published outputs are:

- `geometry_msgs/msg/PoseStamped` for the tag pose relative to the camera frame
- `std_msgs/msg/Float64` for straight-line distance from camera to tag

To keep the system usable before the robot TF tree is finalized, the helper can
bridge the detector's source camera frame under the configured camera frame when
needed.

## Configuration Updates

Updated `launch/robot_config.sh` and `launch/launch_sensors.sh` so the AprilTag
pipeline could be driven from shared configuration.

This includes:

- enabling or disabling AprilTag startup
- selecting the tracked tag ID and family
- setting tag size in meters
- setting pose and distance output topics
- passing calibration file settings through to the camera publisher

## Calibration and Bootstrap Support

The supporting setup now includes:

- camera calibration file loading in `sensor/webcam/publish_camera.sh`
- default calibration path wiring from the robot config
- bootstrap installation of:

```bash
ros-jazzy-apriltag-ros
ros-jazzy-camera-calibration
ros-jazzy-image-proc
```

These changes make the AprilTag stack easier to bring up repeatedly and move it
closer to a future robot-frame pose estimate once the robot geometry and final
TF layout are defined.
